    <string name="help_no_results">No results for “%1$s”.</string>
    <string name="help_hierarchy_title">Card hierarchy</string>
    <string name="help_hierarchy_body">1. 🏳️ Escape (white flag): always loses, unless the trick is only escapes, the Tigress played as an escape or Loots: then the first card played wins.\n2. 🟨🟪🟩 Yellow, purple, green (1 to 14): the suit led beats the other suits.\n3. ⚫ Black trump (Jolly Roger, 1 to 14): beats all suits.\n4. 🧜‍♀️ Mermaids: beat suits and trumps, lose to pirates.\n5. 🏴‍☠️ Pirates: beat mermaids, lose to the Skull King.\n6. 💀 Skull King: beats pirates, but loses to a mermaid.\n\nWith the expansion: Escape &lt; suits &lt; black trump &lt; mermaid &lt; pirates &lt; First Mate Con &lt; Skull King &lt; mermaid. A mermaid beats both First Mate Con and the Skull King.</string>
    <string name="help_special_title">Base game special cards</string>
    <string name="help_special_body">• 🐯 Tigress: played as either a pirate or an escape.\n• 🐙 Kraken: destroys the trick, nobody wins it.\n!> The next trick is led by the player who would have won it without the Kraken (official FAQ).\n• 🐳 White Whale: cancels special cards, the highest numbered card wins.\n• 💰 Loot: played like an escape. It links the player who played it with the winner of the trick: if both make their bid, each of them scores +20.\n> Two Loots can link the same two players: the same alliance can be made twice and each of them can score up to +40.\n!> If a trick starts with a Loot and all the following cards are escapes, the player of the Loot wins the trick: no alliance is formed and no bonus is scored.</string>
    <string name="help_points_title">Points (classic mode)</string>
    <string name="help_points_body">• Bid ≥ 1 made: +20 per bid trick.\n• Bid ≥ 1 missed: −10 per trick off.\n• Zero bid made: +10 × number of cards in the round.\n• Zero bid missed: −10 × number of cards in the round.</string>
    <string name="help_bonus_title">Bonuses</string>
    <string name="help_bonus_body">• 🟨🟪🟩 Suit 14 captured: +10 each\n• ⚫ Black 14 captured: +20\n• 🧜‍♀️ Mermaid captured by a pirate: +20 each\n• 🏴‍☠️ Pirate captured by the Skull King: +30 each\n• 💀 Skull King captured by a mermaid: +40\n• 💰 Loot: +20 if the Loot player and the trick winner both make their bid\n• 🎲 Rascal wager: +wager if the bid is exact, −wager otherwise (0, 10 or 20) — the only term counted even on a missed bid\n!> Bonus points only count if the bid is made.</string>
    <string name="help_modes_title">Scoring modes</string>
    <string name="help_modes_body">• Classic: see above.\n• Rascal (“Direct hit”):\n-- exact bid: 10 × N points plus all bonuses\n-- off by one: 5 × N points plus half the bonuses\n-- off by more: 0 points\n• 💣 Rascal + Cannonball: each player can go “all or nothing” on their bid:\n-- exact bid: 15 × N points plus bonuses\n-- otherwise: 0 points\n-- no wager: the Rascal scoring above applies\n> N is the number of cards dealt in the round.</string>
    <string name="help_expansion_title">2026 expansion</string>
    <string name="help_expansion_body">• 7 captured: −5 each\n• 8 captured: +5 each\n• 0/14 and 🐵 Wild 15: no bonus.\n• {con} First Mate Con: beats all pirates, loses to mermaids and the Skull King. Captured by the Skull King or a mermaid: +30. Scores nothing for captured pirates.\n• 🏴‍☠️ Mary Thorne: counts as a pirate (+30 if captured by the Skull King, +20 per mermaid captured).\n• {davy} Davy Jones’ Locker: doesn’t win, destroys all sea monsters in the trick (🐙 🐳 {ray}): +20 per monster for its player.\n• 🦈 Walk the Plank: removes a pirate from the trick. It scores no bonus.\n• {ray} Spotted Ray: a sea monster, like the Kraken and the White Whale. It doesn’t win the trick: the lowest card in the trick wins. It scores no bonus, and Davy Jones’ Locker can destroy it (+20).\n• 💥 Last Salvo: doesn’t win. Its player plays a 2nd card then skips the last trick.\n!> Like the other bonuses, the expansion ones only count if the bid is made.\n> With 2 players, Wild 15, Walk the Plank and the 0/14s are removed.</string>
    <string name="help_faq_title">FAQ</string>
    <string name="help_faq_body">• Tricks don’t add up to the number of cards? A trick can be destroyed (Kraken, or White Whale / Spotted Ray with no numbered card) or made only of special cards: enter it as a “discarded trick”. The app doesn’t check who won each trick, it only flags inconsistencies and never blocks you.\n• A mistake in a past round? Tap its cell in the scoreboard, then “Correct the round”.\n• No network? No problem, the app works entirely offline.</string>

