    <string name="help_monsters_title">Sea monsters: how play continues</string>
    <string name="help_monsters_body">• **Playing one**: a sea monster (🐙 Kraken, 🐳 White Whale, {ray} Spotted Ray) is a special card: it can be played at any time, even if you could follow the suit. The trick is resolved once everyone has played.\n!> Playing a monster changes nothing about what the other players must play: they still have to follow the suit led (or play a special card). The colors are only ignored when the trick is resolved.\n• 🐙 **Kraken**: nobody wins the trick, its cards are discarded and no bonus is scored (enter it as a “destroyed trick”).\n!> The player who would have won the trick without the Kraken leads the next trick (official FAQ).\n• 🐳 **White Whale**: every special card in the trick (Skull King, pirates, mermaids, Kraken…) counts as an escape, and the numbered cards lose their suit: colors and the black trump no longer matter, only the numbers do. The highest number wins (the first one played in case of a tie), and its player leads the next trick.\n!> If there is no numbered card, the trick is destroyed like with the Kraken, and the player who played the White Whale leads the next trick.\n• {ray} **Spotted Ray** (expansion): it works exactly like the White Whale, except that the lowest number wins instead of the highest.\n• 🐙 🐳 {ray} **Several monsters in the same trick**: only the last monster played takes effect.\n> Whoever wins a trick normally leads the next one. The exceptions are a destroyed trick (nobody wins it) and Rosie D’Laney, who chooses who leads.</string>
    <string name="help_pirates_title">Pirate abilities</string>
    <string name="help_pirates_body">• **Rosie D’Laney**: picks who leads next, including herself.\n• **Rascal of Roatan**: bids 0, 10 or 20 points, added if the bid is made, subtracted if not.\n• **Bendt the Bandit**: draws 2 cards from the draw pile, then discards 2 from their hand.\n• **Juanita Jade**: views the undealt cards to see what is not in play.\n• **Harry the Giant**: adjusts their bid by +1 or −1, or leaves it alone.\n• **Mary Thorne** (expansion): if she wins the trick, her player randomly picks a card from any player’s hand (their own included) without looking at it. That player must play it in the next trick, whatever the suit led.\n> Harry the Giant is the only pirate whose ability also works on the final trick (he must win the trick to activate it).</string>
